   "provider": "Dr. Rachel Colon",
   "specialty": "neurology",
   "page_count": 1,
   "pages": [
    {
     "page": 1,
     "text": "Harris LLC Medical Group\n\nDear Colleague,\n\nI saw Jacqueline Ramos in consultation on May 30, 2025, regarding her ongoing medical conditions. Below is a summary of her evaluation and recommendations.\n\n**History and Examination:**\n\nMs. Ramos presented for a follow-up and medication refill. She reports no recent episodes of concussion symptoms and no new episodes of seizures. She is currently managed with phenytoin 100 mg daily for her epilepsy/seizure disorder. \n\nOn examination, her blood pressure was recorded at 159/103 mmHg, and her weight was 180 lbs. The remainder of her neurological examination was within normal limits with no focal deficits noted. She exhibited normal cranial nerves, motor, and sensory functions, and her coordination and gait were intact.\n\n**Medical Conditions:**\n\n- **Concussion/TBI (residual):**\n Ms. Ramos sustained a concussion and traumatic brain injury on May 10, 2020. At this time, her symptoms are currently controlled without the need for additional medications. She reports no recent headaches, dizziness, or cognitive disturbances.\n\n- **Epilepsy/seizure disorder:**\n Ms. Ramos has a diagnosis of epilepsy with a history of approximately five seizures per year. Notably, she has been seizure-free for 2.3 years since starting on phenytoin 100 mg daily. Her most recent seizure occurred on July 22, 2025. She is compliant with her medication regimen and has not experienced any adverse effects.\n\n**Social History:**\n\n- **Tobacco:**\n Ms. Ramos has a history of smoking one pack per day, which she quit on 18, 2023.\n\n- **Alcohol:**\n She consumes approximately six alcoholic drinks per week.\n\n**Family History:**\n\n- **Mother:**\n Ms. Ramos's mother had a myocardial infarction at the age of 79 and is currently alive.\n\n**Impression and Recommendations:**\n\nMs. Ramos’s current conditions are well-managed with her existing treatment regimen. I recommend continuing her phenytoin 100 mg daily for her epilepsy/seizure disorder. Regular follow-up with her neurologist is advised to monitor her condition and ensure the effectiveness of her treatment.\n\nThank you for referring Ms. Ramos to my care. Please do not hesitate to contact me if there are any further questions or concerns.\n\nSincerely,\n\nDr. Rachel Colon \nNeurology \nHarris LLC Medical Group\n"
    }
   ],
