     "text": "West LLC Clinic\nRe: Jacqueline Ramos (DOB 12/16/1997)\n\nSeptember 22, 2025: Jacqueline Ramos, a 27-year-old female, presented today for follow-up on her epilepsy and seizure disorder. Upon examination, her blood pressure was recorded at 162/103, and she weighed 176 pounds. She continues to do well overall. She is currently being managed with lisinopril 40 mg to control her hypertension, which is within the expected blood pressure band of 161-170/101-105. Additionally, she takes phenytoin 1O0 mg to manage her seizure disorder.\n\nDecember 14, 2024: Jacqueline Ramos was seen for a follow-up her epilepsy and seizure disorder. Her blood pressure was 168/101, and she weighed 179 pounds. She is known to have hypertension, which is being controlled with one medication. She also has a history of a concussion/traumatic brain injury (TBI) with residual effects. \n\nMarch 06, 2024: Jacqueline Ramos visited for an ankle sprain. Her blood pressure was 169/93, and she weighed 186 pounds. She did not report any other concerning symptoms apart from the ankle sprain.\n\nMay 28, 2023: Jacqueline was seen regarding a colon polyp with high-grade dysplasia. Her blood pressure was 165/97, and she weighed 183 pounds. She has known hypertension a concussion/traumatic brain injury with residual effects.\n\nAugust 18,\n"
